      "content": "This selection misses contract-bearing controls whose accessible name omits the contract—the regression the new parity check is meant to catch. For example, `\u003cbutton aria-label=\"Open\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eXYZ Dec 18 $55 Call\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/button\u003e` does not tag the button (its label lacks XYZ and it has children). Only the span is tagged, whose text snapshot is then discarded by the quoted-name parser. The visible-name check passes and the accessible checks never detect the missing contract. Select the semantic elements containing visible contract text regardless of whether their labels already contain XYZ, and compare their computed names even when those names are empty or contain no contract.",
